WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:25.714
EPA 608 is not optional. You cannot legally touch refrigerant without it. Let's
make sure you pass.

00:00:25.714 --> 00:00:51.429
Pressure-temperature fundamentals for EPA 608: every refrigerant has a unique PT
relationship. At the same pressure different refrigerants have different
saturation temperatures. This is why you must know which refrigerant is in the

00:00:51.429 --> 00:01:17.143
Here are the key terms. Write these down.

00:01:17.143 --> 00:01:42.857
Saturation: The condition where liquid and vapor coexist at a given pressure and
temperature.

00:01:42.857 --> 00:02:08.571
Here's why this matters on the job: PT relationships are tested extensively on
the EPA 608 exam.

00:02:08.571 --> 00:02:34.286
Watch out for these: R-410A pressures are much higher than R-22. And — Use
gauges rated for the refrigerant in the system

00:02:34.286 --> 00:03:00.000
Quick check: what is the maximum fine for knowingly venting refrigerant? If you
don't know that number, go back and read it again.

